cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use HBOD, please cite this software release and the paper it accompanies:
  "Development of an autonomous artificial intelligence agent for training load monitoring: a closed-loop in
  silico trial against the acute-to-chronic workload ratio".
title: "HBOD: on-device application, state-space engine and simulation code"
abstract: >-
  HBOD (Hooper-Borg-Oslo-Dergaa) is an autonomous artificial intelligence agent for daily monitoring of training
  load, wellness and health. This release holds the HBOD web application, which computes on the coach's device
  without uploading any data, its state-space engine (a Kalman filter with athlete-specific learning by recursive
  least squares that reports a probability), the complete simulation code of the paper (Supplementary File S1) and
  the parity test of the JavaScript engine against the Python code of File S1.
type: software
